{"rare":{"w":"rare","zh":["稀少","稀疏","稀有","罕見","一分熟"],"ipa":{"uk":"/ɹɛə/","us":"/ɹɛɚ/"},"ety":[{"n":1,"chain":[{"l":"enm","f":"rare","t":"inh"},{"l":"fro","f":"rare","t":"der"},{"l":"la","f":"rārus","t":"der","g":"loose, spaced apart, thin, infrequent"},{"l":"ine-pro","f":"*h₁reh₁-","t":"der","g":"friable, thin"}],"text":"From Middle English rare, from Old French rare, rere (“rare, uncommon”), from Latin rārus (“loose, spaced apart, thin, infrequent”), from Proto-Indo-European *h₁reh₁- (“friable, thin”). Displaced native English geason (“rare, scarce”) (from Middle English gesen, from Old English gǣsne); and largely displaced Middle English seld (“rare, uncommon”) (from Old English selden) and Middle English seldscene (“rare, rarely seen, infrequent”) (from Old English seldsēne) hence modern English seld"},{"n":2,"chain":[{"l":"enm","f":"rere","t":"inh"},{"l":"ang","f":"hrēr","t":"inh"},{"l":"gem-pro","f":"*hrōzijaną","t":"der","g":"to stir"},{"l":"ine-pro","f":"*ḱroHs-","t":"der","g":"to mix, stir, cook"}],"text":"From a dialectal variant of rear, from Middle English rere, from Old English hrēr, hrēre (“not thoroughly cooked, underdone, lightly boiled”), from hrēran (“to move, shake, agitate”), from Proto-Germanic *hrōzijaną (“to stir”), from Proto-Indo-European *ḱroHs- (“to mix, stir, cook”). Related to Old English hrōr (“stirring, busy, active, strong, brave”). More at rear.","cog":[{"l":"ang","f":"hrōr"}]},{"n":3,"chain":[],"text":"Variant of rear."},{"n":4,"chain":[],"text":"Compare rather, rath."}],"pos":[{"p":"adj","e":0,"senses":[{"d":"Very uncommon; scarce.","ex":["Black pearls are very rare and therefore very valuable."],"syn":["scarce","selcouth","seld","selly","geason","uncommon"],"grp":0,"zh":"稀少；稀疏；稀有"},{"d":"Small in number (but not unusual); infrequent; sparse.","tags":["medicine"]},{"d":"Thin; of low density.","grp":1},{"d":"Good; enjoyable.","tags":["British","slang"],"ex":["Sees her reflection in a butcher shop.\nShe finds it all quite rare\nThat her meat's all vanity fair."]},{"d":"Cool; excellent.","tags":["US","slang"],"ex":["I whistled for a cab and when it came near / The license plate said ‘fresh’ and it had dice in the mirror. / If anything I could say that this cab was rare."]}],"forms":[["comp","rarer"],["sup","rarest"]]},{"p":"noun","e":0,"senses":[{"d":"A scarce or uncommon item."}],"forms":[["pl","rares"]]},{"p":"adj","e":1,"senses":[{"d":"Particularly of meat, especially beefsteak: cooked very lightly, so the meat is still red.","grp":2,"zh":"一分熟"}],"forms":[["comp","rarer"],["comp","more rare"],["sup","rarest"],["sup","most rare"]]},{"p":"verb","e":2,"senses":[{"d":"To rear, rise up, start backwards.","tags":["US","intransitive"],"ex":["Frank pretended to rare back as if bedazzled, shielding his eyes with a forearm."]},{"d":"To rear, bring up, raise.","tags":["US","transitive"]}],"forms":[["3s","rares"],["ing","raring"],["pp","rared"],["past","rared"]]},{"p":"adj","e":3,"senses":[{"d":"Early.","tags":["obsolete"],"ex":["The men, that sway / In work of those tools that so fit our state, / Are rude mechanicals, that rare and late / Work in the market-place;"]}],"forms":[["comp","more rare"],["sup","most rare"]]}],"grp":[{"label":"very uncommon","zh":["稀少","稀疏","稀有","罕見"],"p":"adj","e":0,"tr":{"fr":["fr:rare","fr:peu commun"],"it":["it:raro"],"es":["es:raro","es:insólito","es:ralo"],"pt":["pt:raro"]}},{"label":"thin density gas","zh":[],"p":"adj","e":0,"tr":{"fr":[],"it":[],"es":["es:ralo"],"pt":["pt:rarefeito"]}},{"label":"cooked very lightly","zh":["一分熟"],"p":"adj","e":1,"tr":{"fr":["fr:saignant"],"it":["it:al sangue"],"es":["es:crudo","es:poco hecho","es:jugoso"],"pt":["pt:malpassado"]}}],"lx":{"fr:rare":{"w":"rare","p":"adj","pl":"rares","ipa":"/ʁaʁ/","gl":"rare","ety":{"chain":[{"l":"la","f":"rārus","t":"bor","g":"Rarus (father of Triptolemus)"},{"l":"grc","f":"Ρ̓ᾶρος","t":"bor"}],"text":"Borrowed (in this form) from Latin rārus. Compare the inherited Old French rer, rere."}},"fr:peu commun":{